# Copy to a PRIVATE target .env (mode 0600). Every example remains commented.
# Never commit actual values.

# Immutable release only. Candidate observed on Hostinger source, not yet approved
# for the target (verify upstream provenance, edition and platform first):
# WAHA_IMAGE_DIGEST=41283bd89922ec3f722e5a772b844c451634d4aa72e9c34043c3480184f970fe
# WAHA_ENGINE=NOWEB
#
# Provenance decision 2026-10-07 (P3 tranche 3): the source digest above could
# NOT be attributed to any upstream amd64 manifest (noweb/gows/chrome/latest
# 2026.9.1, noweb/gows 2026.9.2, current latest) and the source pulls by
# floating `:latest` (empty RepoDigests). DO NOT reuse it. Approved target pin
# (evidence: upstream tag/edition/platform/push-date verified 2026-10-07):
# upstream tag noweb-2026.9.2 (amd64 manifest sha256:0999fb384426222be591f3ffd15879f39b8940662df2f9f1d70d836a8315f659,
# pushed 2026-10-02), engine NOWEB (matches the source live config, no browser
# dependency). RepoDigest verification is AUTOMATED in deploy-waha.sh (it
# compares the pulled RepoDigests with the pinned value and aborts before
# `up`), but that script has never been executed: until a first verified run is
# recorded, treat the comparison as MANUAL and abort on any mismatch.

# The server stores only this hash; the corresponding plain key is a separate
# server-side app secret. Do not copy the source key.
# WAHA_API_KEY_HASH=sha512:<128-lowercase-hex-digest>
# WAHA_SWAGGER_USERNAME=<private-user>
# WAHA_SWAGGER_PASSWORD=<random-secret-at-least-24-chars>
#
# Values must stay in the shared safe charset [A-Za-z0-9._:/-]: no quotes, no
# spaces, no inline comments and no `$` interpolation. Both `preflight.mjs` and
# `deploy-waha.sh` parse the file declaratively (never `source` it), so those
# forms are rejected instead of executed.

# A private HMAC key is required by the candidate, even while the hook URL is
# blank. Set WAHA_WEBHOOK_URL only after an enabled app installation exists.
# WAHA_WEBHOOK_HMAC_KEY=<random-base64url-or-hex-secret-at-least-32-chars>
# Accepted form (same rule in preflight.mjs and deploy-waha.sh):
# https://<host>[:<port>]/api/whatsapp/waha — e.g. https://127.0.0.1:3000/api/whatsapp/waha
# Path must be exact in the raw value (dot segments are rejected); host must be a
# DNS name or a canonical IPv4 quad; port 0-65535 without leading zeros.
# A final WHATWG hexadecimal-number label is rejected as well — `0x7f`,
# `1.2.3.0xff`, `example.0xff` and their zero-hex-digit forms (`0x`, `0X`,
# `1.2.3.0x`, `example.0x`) — because the parser would renormalize the host or
# fail the authority. A legal DNS label such as `0xapp` stays valid.
# WAHA_WEBHOOK_URL=
